        "title": "Oral History as Method: Interview Technique, Archive, Reliability",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**The critical distinction**: oral history methodology was developed to record living memory before it is lost — a documentary act. Oral tradition is a living community practice that the researcher studies. Confusing the two produces methodological errors in both directions."
    },
